  dialogueText: 'Now we''re moving into a more advanced part of Ilokano.


    In
    a sentence, the word ''ket'' can connect the subject with information that describes
    it.


    Think of ''ket'' as a connector that helps link the two parts of the
    sentence.


    Listen carefully: ket.


    Now, try saying ''ket'' yourself.'
